{"input":{"file_path":"/home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tactics.md"},"kind":"tool","name":"Read","output":"1\t---\n2\tname: rct2-coaster-contest-tactics\n3\tdescription: What actually moves excitement in the RCT2 steel-twister (ride_type 51) building contest\n4\tmetadata: \n5\t  node_type: memory\n6\t  type: project\n7\t  originSessionId: 9566f1cd-bad2-469e-b14f-fe34a6cccace\n8\t  modified: 2026-07-24T19:24:24.934Z\n9\t---\n10\t\n11\tMulti-round RCT2 coaster contest via the `coaster` MCP tools. Measured results, rounds 3-5.\n12\t\n13\t**Scoreboard so far: 7.13 @ intensity 10.17 (round 4) is still the all-time best. Round 5 topped out at 6.94 @ intensity 8.19.**\n14\t\n15\tRound-5 measurements, all on one 125-piece layout where only the hill/drop profile changed:\n16\t\n17\t| build | drop1 | drop2 | inversions | air | excitement | intensity |\n18\t|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n19\t| v1 | 192 | 208 | 4 | 64 | 6.74 | 7.42 |\n20\t| v2 | 240 (2x down_60) | 208 | 5 | 105 | **5.22** | **10.49** |\n21\t| v3 | 192 | 192 | 5 | 95 | 6.88 | 8.02 |\n22\t| v4 | 208 | 208 | 5 | 94 | **6.94** | 8.19 |\n23\t| v5 | 208 | 208 | 6 | 74 | 6.93 | 8.55 |\n24\t\n25\t- **Two consecutive `down_60` pieces in one drop is the intensity bomb**: +2.3 intensity (8.19 -> 10.49) for only +4 `highest_drop`. Never chain two. One `down_60` with a 3-piece 25-degree pullout is safe.\n26\t- **Drop depth on its own is cheap**: deepening both drops 192 -> 208 cost only +0.17 intensity. Height is not what spikes intensity; sustained 60-degree freefall is.\n27\t- **A 6th inversion is not free**: v5 bought one by deleting airtime hops from the return leg and landed exactly where v4 did. Airtime hops and inversions trade roughly 1:1, so add inversions only in space the hops were not using.\n28\t- **The intensity/excitement curve is NOT simply \"stay under 10.\"** 10.17 scored 7.13 but 10.49 scored 5.22, while 8.19 only scored 6.94. The sweet spot looks like **intensity 9.8-10.2** — right at the edge, not comfortably below it. Round 5's mistake was over-correcting to 8.2 and leaving ~2 points of headroom unspent. Next round: rebuild v4 and climb intensity in small steps (deeper drops, more inversions, a helix) aiming to land at ~10.1, testing after each step.\n29\t- Similarity stays 0.30-0.39 with these layouts, safely under the 0.5 penalty.\n30\t\n31\t**Geometry / how to build:** `piece_geometry` returns dir-0 deltas only; rotate with R(x,y) = (y,-x) applied k times for facing k, and dir_out = (dir_out_at_0 + k) mod 4. Planning the whole circuit on paper this way closed the circuit first try on all four round-5 builds. Reliable skeleton: station at (60,60) facing dir 0 -> lift/drop/loop west -> banked right turn -> second chain lift heading +y -> drop -> right turn -> inversion cluster heading +x -> right turn -> `s_bend_left` diagonal back (each is +1x,-3y at dir 3) -> brakes -> `right_turn_5` from (63,62) dir 3 lands exactly on (60,60) dir 0. To retune hill height without breaking closure, keep the piece *count* per leg fixed and pad with `flat` — dz changes, dx/dy do not.\n32\t","seq":2,"status":"completed"}
