{"input":{"file_path":"/home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tactics.md","new_string":"**Scoreboard: 7.13 @ intensity 10.17 (round 4) is still the all-time best. Round 6 = 7.07 @ 8.08. Round 5 = 6.94 @ 8.19.**\n\n**Round-6 findings — the \"raise intensity to ~10\" plan FAILED to find a working lever. Three dead ends, all confirmed by measurement:**\n- **A 360-degree helix is unbuildable on this coaster.** Both `*_helix_up_large` + `*_helix_down_large` AND two consecutive `*_helix_up_large` are rejected with \"Twister Roller Coaster 1 in the way\" — 16 units of climb per 180-degree half is not enough vertical clearance to stack. Small helices fail identically. Helix pieces are only usable as *single* 180-degree half-turns (i.e. just a banked turn that gains/loses 16), which is not an intensity lever. Do not spend time here again.\n- **Unbanked turns change NOTHING.** Swapping `flat_to_right_bank`/`banked_right_turn_5`/`right_bank_to_flat` for `flat`/`right_turn_5`/`flat` (identical geometry, drop-in substitution) at two high-speed turns produced a byte-identical eval report: same 7.07 / 8.08 / max_lateral_g 2.80. Lateral G was already saturated at 2.8 from the corkscrews/s-bends. Banking is free to change and irrelevant to the rating.\n- **`half_loop_up` + `half_loop_down` cannot follow a drop.** It needs a 25-up entry (`flat_to_up_25` first, `down_25_to_flat` after), which makes the 4-piece block net exactly 4 flats — geometrically perfect drop-in. But the half loop *reverses direction*, so it always folds back over the track you just arrived on: \"in the way\". Only placeable coming out of a turn with clear space behind, where speed is too low to clear its 152 units of climb. Probably not worth retrying.\n\n**Inversions are counted in PAIRS.** 2 vertical loops + 6 corkscrew pieces reported `num_inversions: 5`, not 8. A corkscrew inversion = `X_corkscrew_up` + `Y_corkscrew_down` together. Budget 2 pieces per corkscrew inversion.\n\nRound-6 layout (7.07, 114 pieces, similarity 0.33) beat round 5 by simplifying, not by adding: two 208-unit lifts/drops, 2 vertical loops, 3 corkscrew inversions, 14 drops, air 78. Versus round 5's 6.94 it cut ~11 pieces of dead return-leg straight. **Shorter dead track = more excitement** may be the real lever, not intensity.\n\nNext round: stop chasing intensity via G-forces (levers are exhausted). Instead try (a) deepening both drops 208 -> 288 for `highest_drop`/max_speed, compensating the +5-tiles-per-leg shift in the s-bend return leg, and (b) cutting more dead flat/s-bend track.","old_string":"**Scoreboard so far: 7.13 @ intensity 10.17 (round 4) is still the all-time best. Round 5 topped out at 6.94 @ intensity 8.19.**","replace_all":false},"kind":"tool","name":"Edit","output":"The file /home/sandbox/.claude/projects/-workspace/memory/rct2-coaster-contest-tactics.md has been updated successfully.","seq":41,"status":"completed"}
